From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:58:57 -0400
Subject: fix: no Google sign-in at first run, an even sidebar foot, a shadow
 under the command bar

Browser sign-in is never offered (privacy Q16, GitHub issue 38). Chromium
allows it wherever an OAuth client is configured, and the
GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET environment
variables, which guides for Chromium builds tell people to set, configure
one. Windows apps see the user's environment, so Stedding there asked to
sign in to Google at the first start; apps opened from the Mac's Finder
do not, so the Mac did not. Chromium's own first run, the screen that
asked, never opens either: Stedding's welcome is the first start
(welcome W18).

The sidebar's foot: History moves from the bottom row to the Archived
row's line, at its end with its icon over the "+"; the line is shorter,
its text two sizes under the rows' and at half their strength. The
bottom row keeps the downloads button and the "+" at its ends, and the
Space chips centre on the whole row, not on what the button leaves them
(sidebar Y44, the owner).

The command bar casts a shadow and has a hairline edge, so it stands off
a white page in the light look (commandbar K36, GitHub issue 37).

Why: GitHub issues 38 and 37, and the owner on the sidebar's foot
(2026-10-25).
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the code.
